### 2. REQUIRED TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following stack unless a documented technical limitation requires an alternative.

#### Frontend
- Next.js with App Router.
- React.
- TypeScript with strict mode.
- Tailwind CSS.
- shadcn/ui for accessible interface components.
- Lucide React icons.
- React Hook Form.
- Zod validation.
- Framer Motion for interface transitions.

#### 3D rendering
- Three.js.
- React Three Fiber.
- @react-three/drei.
- GLSL shaders only where they provide meaningful visual improvements.
- GLTF/GLB models for optimized 3D assets.
- WebP or AVIF textures when appropriate.
- Instanced meshes and level-of-detail techniques for complex scenes.

#### Backend
- Next.js server-side route handlers.
- Server-side validation.
- A dedicated service layer.
- Secure authentication and authorization.
- Centralized error handling.
- Rate limiting and request-size limits.

#### AI
- Google Gemini API for AI itinerary generation.
- The official Google Gen AI SDK compatible with the selected Gemini model.
- Structured JSON output validated with Zod.
- A dedicated Gemini service module.
- Controlled retries, timeouts, and usage limits.

Use the current supported Gemini model available to the configured API account. Make the model configurable through server-side environment variables rather than hardcoding an obsolete model name.

#### Database and authentication
- Supabase PostgreSQL.
- Supabase Auth.
- Row-level security.
- Version-controlled SQL migrations.
- Supabase Storage only when required.

#### Maps and weather
- Google Maps Platform for places, maps, and routes, or a documented equivalent.
- A configurable weather provider.
- Provider-backed geocoding and route information.

#### Deployment
- Vercel-compatible configuration.
- Git-based version control.
- ESLint and TypeScript checks.
- Automated tests.
- A complete README and .env.example.

Never expose Gemini credentials, Supabase service-role credentials, invitation secrets, or privileged provider keys in browser code.

